-- 
2. Bonesaw core-patch series

V2 (#126): TRUE personal loot - per-member lootable, no overlap
---------------------------------------------------------------
Player feedback on the v1 behaviour: "loot isn't personal, it's just FFA, not
the same thing at all. i want everyone to be able to loot every corpse without
any overlap (but only 1 person can skin stuff still)."

v1 only changed WHO MAY LOOT the single shared set of drops (first come first
served, items vanished for everyone once taken). v2 changes WHAT LOOTING MEANS:

CHOSEN DESIGN (b) - shared roll, per-member lootable views
----------------------------------------------------------
The loot table is still rolled ONCE per kill (the drop list is identical for
every member; no extra dice, no retail-style independent rolls). What changes
is that every dropped item becomes MULTI-LOOTABLE: each eligible group member
gets their own view of the full drop table and loots each item once; what one
member takes does not disappear for anyone else. This matches the request
("everyone can loot every corpse without any overlap") without inventing new
loot-storage machinery, by reusing the exact per-player view mechanism
AzerothCore already uses for MULTI_DROP (FFA) items.

MECHANISM
---------
- New config "Loot.PersonalLootDuplicate" (CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_DUPLICATE,
  default ON), documented below. Only evaluated when Loot.PersonalLootAll is
  also on - the two options together define the Bonesaw loot policy.
- Loot::FillLoot (group branch, i.e. creature corpses and group-rules chests):
  when the option is on, every generated non-quest item is flagged
  freeforall = true before the per-player views are filled.
- Flagging freeforall routes each item through the per-player FFA view system:
  Loot::FillFFALoot() creates a QuestItemList per member in
  Loot::PlayerFFAItems (index + per-member is_looted flag), the LootView
  serializer shows each viewer THEIR OWN view entries, Loot::LootItemInSlot
  resolves looted-state per member, and Player::StoreLootItem takes the
  ffaitem branch: it sets only the member's QuestItem::is_looted and notifies
  only that member (SendNotifyLootItemRemoved) - the shared LootItem is never
  globally marked looted (the `if (!item->freeforall) item->is_looted = true`
  guard skips it). So: member A loots the sword; members B and C still see it
  and can loot their own copy. No overlap, no rolls, no fighting.
- unlootedCount bookkeeping stays balanced (FillFFALoot increments per member
  per item, each member's loot decrements once), so corpses still release when
  everyone has taken everything. Because the per-member count can now reach
  items x members (raids), unlootedCount was widened uint8 -> uint32.
- Members who were not in loot-reward distance when the loot was generated get
  their views lazily: Player::SendLoot (creature branch) now calls
  loot->FillNotNormalLootFor(this) for corpse loot when the option is on
  (no-op if views already exist). Without this, a freeforall corpse would show
  NOTHING to a player not filled at kill time (the ALL_PERMISSION serializer
  only renders freeforall items through the per-player views).
- Gold is untouched: one pool, HandleLootMoneyOpcode splits it once.
- Quest items / conditional items are untouched: already per-player views.
- SKINNING STAYS ONE-TAKER, verified twice over: skinning loot is generated by
  a separate FillLoot(..., personal = true) call (Player::SendLoot, LOOT_
  SKINNING) which never enters the group branch, so its items are never
  flagged freeforall; and Player::isAllowedToLoot returns the skinning corpse
  to the loot recipient only (loot_type == LOOT_SKINNING early return).
  The skinning ACTION also remains first-come (creature skinning state).
- Loot.PersonalLootAll (v1) keeps doing its job underneath: it is what makes
  every group member eligible (ALL_PERMISSION, isAllowedToLoot, no rolls).

FILES (v2 additions)
--------------------
 src/server/game/World/WorldConfig.h          | CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_DUPLICATE
 src/server/game/World/WorldConfig.cpp        | register Loot.PersonalLootDuplicate (true)
 src/server/game/Loot/LootMgr.h               | unlootedCount uint8 -> uint32
 src/server/game/Loot/LootMgr.cpp             | FillLoot freeforall flagging
 src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp   | SendLoot lazy per-member view fill
                                                | + GO-chest reopen switch -> GetEffectiveLootMethod()

CONFIG
------
 Loot.PersonalLootDuplicate = 1 (default)
     When Loot.PersonalLootAll is also enabled, every dropped item from a
     group kill/chest is lootable once by EACH eligible group member
     (per-member views of one shared roll; no overlap, gold splits once,
     skinning stays single-taker). 0 restores v1 first-come-first-served FFA.

